<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 44,090 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 44,090 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-02-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 44,090 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Sunday, compared to 37,195 tonnes on Saturday.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>					    Sunday	    Previous</p>
<p>    Export cargo			26,636	    12,446</p>
<p>    Import cargo			17,454	    24,749</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, ten ships sailed and seven berthed. In the next 24 hours, seven ships were expected to sail and five to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at the Karachi Port:</p>
<p>Commodity	     Tonnes/TEUs  Ship		   Berthing</p>
<p>High speed diesel   3,000	  Chesapeak City     18/2</p>
<p>Crude oil	     70,000	 Stavros		18/2</p>
<p>High speed diesel   56,000	 Keefan		 due</p>
<p>Sulphur		 3,900	  Sea Princess	 due</p>
<p>High speed diesel   56,000	 Warbah		 due</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
